@startuml
title Deploying one KMS party
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ActorBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ActorBorderColor #7A5BB5
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F5FC
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
autonumber

actor "Party operator" as Op
participant "Terraform\n(terraform-mpc-modules)" as TF
participant "AWS account\nEKS, S3, IAM, KMS, PrivateLink" as AWS
participant "Helm\nkms-core chart" as Helm
participant "kms-server\n(Nitro Enclave)" as KMS
participant "Other 12 parties" as Peers
participant "Gateway" as GW

Op -> TF : party ID, tfvars\n(c7a.16xlarge, enclave, attestation SHA)
TF -> AWS : EKS + enclave node group,\n2 S3 buckets, IRSA roles, KMS root key
Op -> TF : PrivateLink provider + consumer
TF -> AWS : VPC endpoint service,\nendpoints to 12 parties
Op -> Peers : exchange service names,\nTLS certificates (out of band)
Op -> Helm : values: peersList, PCR allowlist,\nthreshold params, vaults
Helm -> KMS : StatefulSet, enclave 48 CPU / 96 GiB
Op -> KMS : kms-gen-keys\n(seed, ECDSA key, TLS cert)
KMS -> AWS : seed and key to private vault + backup
Op -> GW : register party\n(signer address, public storage)
Op -> KMS : kms-init (PRSS, once per party set)
KMS <-> Peers : PRSS setup over attested mTLS
GW -> KMS : preprocessing, KeyGen, CrsGen\n(via connector, hours)
KMS <-> Peers : distributed key generation
KMS -> AWS : shares to private vault,\npublic keys to Keychain DA
KMS -> GW : signed digests
note over KMS, Peers #F8F5FC : Port 50100 stays on localhost; 50001 only between parties;\n9646 only to monitoring.
@enduml
